Short Viva Answers

1. What is handoff?

Transfer of ongoing call from one base station to another.


---

2. Why is handoff required?

To maintain continuous communication when user moves.


---

3. What is hard handoff?

Old connection breaks before new connection forms.


---

4. What is soft handoff?

New connection forms before old connection breaks.


---

5. What causes handoff?

Movement of mobile user between cells.


---

6. What is call drop?

Unexpected disconnection of active call.


---

7. What is outage probability?

Probability that signal strength falls below threshold.


---

8. What is SNR?

Signal-to-Noise Ratio.


---

9. What happens when SNR increases?

Communication quality improves.


---

10. Which handoff is used in GSM?

Hard handoff.


---

11. Which handoff is used in CDMA?

Soft handoff.


---

12. What is co-channel interference?

Interference caused by same frequency reuse in nearby cells.


---

13. What is frequency reuse?

Using same frequency channels in different cells.


---

14. What is cell radius?

Coverage area of a base station.


---

15. Advantage of handoff?

Provides uninterrupted communication.
